{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1815","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1815","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1815\",\"parent_revision\":\"42d74a2d9aba1ca2577c7dc38390ee7891d6e6ac2929521696b75e89b4237fb1\",\"root_revision\":\"42d74a2d9aba1ca2577c7dc38390ee7891d6e6ac2929521696b75e89b4237fb1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWithout an explicit `tools:` declaration, task-worker inherits the default (all tools) or the parent orchestrator's permissions at runtime. The behavior is not observable from the agent file itself, so:\\n\\n- The CLAUDE.md claim that task-worker \\\"carries full dh tool permissions\\\" is not independently verifiable from the agent configuration\\n- Future platform changes to default tool inheritance could silently remove SAM MCP or backlog MCP from task-worker without any agent-file change being required\\n- Plugin linters that check agent-to-MCP tool alignment cannot verify task-worker's declared-vs-actual permissions\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` frontmatter contains a `tools:` field listing at minimum the SAM MCP tools and backlog MCP tools that CLAUDE.md claims the agent has\\n- [ ] Pre-commit or plugin-lint check confirms the tools list matches the pattern used by other dh agents\\n- [ ] No behavioral regression \u2014 existing skills that dispatch task-worker still work after the frontmatter change\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: task-worker.md frontmatter missing tools field despite claude.md asserting full dh mcp permissions** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered 2026-04-14 during regroom of #1774 (fact-checker REFUTED Claim 5)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-14\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` has no `tools:` field in its YAML frontmatter, despite `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` lines 195-199 asserting the agent \\\"carries full dh tool permissions (SAM MCP, backlog MCP)\\\". 13 other agents in `plugins/development-harness/agents/` explicitly declare `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__*` and `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__*` tools in their frontmatter; task-worker is the only dh agent with no tools declaration at all.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nDiscovered 2026-04-14 during regroom of #1774 (corrected task-worker premise). Fact-checker ran `Read plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` and found no `tools:` key in the frontmatter, then cross-checked 13 other agent files which all declare MCP tool access explicitly.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\ntask-worker.md frontmatter should explicitly declare the MCP tools it requires:\\n\\n- `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_task`\\n- `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan`\\n- `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_active_task`\\n- `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__*` (the set required for claim/state/update lifecycle)\\n- `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__profile_load`\\n\\nMatching the pattern used by the 13 other agent files in the same directory.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #1774 \u2014 the regroom of the dispatch-discipline item where this gap was discovered. #1774's RT-ICA condition 8 (scope of task-worker.md frontmatter fix) is resolved by spinning out this defect as a separate item.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c2e1fbeb6ac406a1bae2316164edf5b9805f629a9cf5dd83f7a31dc41c472c8b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCyJQA\"}"}